 "editor_notes": [
  "¶1 (\"גם יש להבין הראי' ... מזה הא' לולי ה'\"): הא' expanded as הָאוֹמֵר (\"this [verse] that says\"); the abbreviation could also stand for הָאָמוּר. Meaning unaffected.",
  "¶2 (\"(חגיגה יד. וש\"מ)\"): וש\"מ expanded as וּשְׁאָר מְקוֹמוֹת (\"and elsewhere\"); possibly intended as וש\"נ (ושם נסמן). Uncertain.",
  "¶2 (Shabbat meals, \"נתקן פגם הכעם והקנאה\"): הכעם is a print error for הכעס (anger); printed reading kept and vocalized הַכַּעַם, translated \"anger\". Suggested correction: הַכַּעַס.",
  "¶1 (\"והנה אי' בגמ' (סוכה נג.)\"): the passage of David and the deep begins at the bottom of Sukkah 53a and continues on 53b (the words כמה דמידלי טפי מירטב עלמא are on 53b). Citation kept as printed.",
  "¶1 (\"מ\"ט לולי ה' שהיה לנו יאמר ישראל סבא\"): the second quotation of Tehillim 124:1 omits נא (shorthand); kept as printed. The (שם) after \"אמרו ז\"ל\" refers to Sukkah; the saying \"אם פגע בך מנוול זה\" is at Sukkah 52b.",
  "¶2 (\"בת שבע בתו\"): so also the Gemara (Sanhedrin 101b); Bat Sheva was Achitofel's granddaughter (bat bito), hence \"[grand]daughter\" in the English."
 ]
